Experiment: Model a Machine Using Python Classes
Course: CS-1281 | Python Programming Lab
Department: Production Engineering, VSSUT Burla
Date: 04-09-2026

1. Aim
To understand Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) and develop a machine model using Python classes and objects.

2. Objectives
IT12: Create a machine class with attributes, constructor, __str__() and working methods.
IT10: Implement private attributes, validation and status getter methods.
IT8: Process a batch of 10 jobs and generate a shift report.
IT6: Manage three machines using a list and generate a fleet report.
3. Concepts Used
Classes and objects
Constructor (__init__)
Attributes and methods
Encapsulation and private variables
Validation and getter methods
Lists and loops
max() and lambda functions
Python modules and imports
4. Machine Design
Example: Hydraulic Press

Attributes:

Machine name
Capacity
Operating speed
Machine status
Parts produced
Methods:

start() – Starts the machine.
stop() – Stops the machine.
operate() – Processes a part.
status() – Displays machine condition.
__str__() – Displays machine information.
5. Inspection and Testing
Check machine initialization.
Test commands beyond machine capacity.
Prevent operation when the machine is stopped.
Check independent objects.
Test whether private data can be modified externally.
6. Fleet Management
Three machine objects are stored in a list. Jobs are allocated to available machines, and the final report displays:

Parts produced by each machine.
Total plant production.
Busiest machine.
7. Result
Successfully studied Python classes, objects, encapsulation and methods to develop a machine model and manage production operations.

8. Conclusion
Object-Oriented Programming helps represent real industrial machines through reusable classes and objects. It improves code organization, data protection and maintainability.
